    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7146f970_49c2324f",
        "filename": "bbsim/templates/deployment.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000569
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-08T17:17:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "are we talking about docker tags? the change is essential to add parameters which were added to the binary but not yet added in the helm chart (which is the case right now)\nI don\u0027t understand the cons of this change for me it\u0027s ideal. Let me give an example:\nthe binary supports right now rest_api_address parameter which is quite useful. But it\u0027s completely missing in helm. All I need to do is to call --set .args.rest_api_address\u003d:50442 (I am not sure about the syntax but you understand the idea) when installing the chart and the binary will expose the needed port, In another situation a programmer of bbsim will add parameter xyz but will forget to add it to the helm (which happened in the past). So to get it in the helm we have to wait couple of weeks till community reviews the changes and merges them to the helm repository. In our situation I\u0027ll just add --set args.xyz\u003d123 to our installation script and everything works instantly without any delays!",
      "parentUuid": "f2be43e0_aa5f7bae",
      "revId": "202565990bfb6521844de9ee00c69ca3da03cd36",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a765439_1b0f050a",
        "filename": "bbsim/templates/deployment.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000007
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-08T21:59:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason to have the explicit parameters in the helm chart is to make it easier for the user to know which configurations are exposed and he can control. If we introduce that loop what will happen is that no-one will ever change the chart again to support new flags, thus whoever install it needs to go check in the binary which options are supported.\n\nThe most obvious downside is that if someone removes a parameter that you have defined in your installation script then the installation will fail with an error like: \"flag provided but not defined: -c_tag\"\n\nUltimately what I\u0027m suggesting is to just add this (instead of the loop):\n+            \"-rest_api_address\", \"{{ .Values.bbsim_rest_port }}\",",
      "parentUuid": "7146f970_49c2324f",
      "revId": "202565990bfb6521844de9ee00c69ca3da03cd36",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": true
    },
